# Proxy List Example
# ==================
# Copy this file to 'proxies.txt' and add your actual proxies
# Format: [protocol://][username:password@]host:port
#
# Supported protocols: http, https, socks4, socks5
# If no protocol specified, http is assumed

# ==================
# HTTP Proxies
# ==================

# Simple HTTP proxy (no authentication)
# http://proxy1.example.com:8080
# http://proxy2.example.com:3128

# HTTP proxy with authentication
# http://username:password@proxy3.example.com:8080

# ==================
# SOCKS Proxies
# ==================

# SOCKS5 proxy
# socks5://proxy4.example.com:1080

# SOCKS5 with authentication
# socks5://username:password@proxy5.example.com:1080

# ==================
# No Protocol (assumes HTTP)
# ==================

# Short format - assumes http://
# proxy6.example.com:8080
# proxy7.example.com:3128

# ==================
# Where to Get Proxies
# ==================
#
# FREE (not recommended for production):
# - https://www.proxy-list.download/
# - https://free-proxy-list.net/
# - https://www.sslproxies.org/
#
# PAID (recommended for production):
# - Bright Data (brightdata.com) - $500+/month
# - Oxylabs (oxylabs.io) - $300+/month
# - SmartProxy (smartproxy.com) - $75+/month
# - ProxyMesh (proxymesh.com) - $20+/month
# - WebShare (webshare.io) - $10+/month
#
# ==================
# Testing Your Proxies
# ==================
#
# Test a proxy with curl:
#   curl -x http://proxy:port https://api.ipify.org
#
# Should return proxy's IP address, not your real IP
#
# Test with Python:
#   import requests
#   proxies = {'http': 'http://proxy:port', 'https': 'http://proxy:port'}
#   response = requests.get('https://api.ipify.org', proxies=proxies)
#   print(response.text)  # Proxy IP
#
# ==================
# Proxy Rotation Tips
# ==================
#
# 1. Mix of different proxy providers (better distribution)
# 2. Monitor performance (remove slow/dead proxies)
# 3. Use 'round_robin' for even distribution
# 4. Use 'random' to avoid detection patterns
# 5. Keep proxy list updated (proxies die often)
#
